# ── AttendX Frontend ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy: cp .env.example .env   (optional — the defaults work everywhere)
#
# The app calls the API on ITS OWN origin under /api/…  (same-origin mode):
#   • npm run dev  → Vite proxies /api → http://127.0.0.1:3000  (vite.config.js)
#   • Docker       → nginx proxies  /api → server:3000          (nginx.conf)
#   • Project IDX / Firebase Studio → open ONLY the 5173 preview; nothing else
# So there is no CORS to configure and VITE_API_URL can stay EMPTY.
#
# API running on another port locally?  (dev server only)
# API_PROXY_TARGET=http://127.0.0.1:4000
#
# API deliberately hosted on a different domain (e.g. Netlify UI + Render API)?
# Then set the full URL and allow that origin on the API (FRONTEND_URL / CORS_OPEN):
# VITE_API_URL=https://attendx-api.example.com
